er limit affects caching or if search without limit vs with limit uses separate cache entries or if limit is part of search cache key / bypassed. Wait, let's look at how `Table.search` uses cache).\\n\"\n}"}, {"step": 6, "role": "Designer", "reply": "{\"action\": \"read_file\", \"path\": \"tinydb/table.py\", \"start_line\": "}, {"step": 7, "role": "Designer", "reply": "{\n  \"action\": \"finish\",\n  \"result\": {\n    \"all_pass\": true,\n    \"blocked\": false,\n    \"classification\": \"feature\",\n    \"summary\": \"Designed the implementation plan to add an optional limit parameter to Table.search and TinyDB.search.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"success\"\n  }\n}"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 352741, "completion_tokens": 23546, "total_tokens": 378330, "calls": 29, "fallbacks": 18, "models": {"gemini-3.5-flash": 11, "gemini-3.5-flash-lite": 18}}}